Hi. 

I'm bumping this thread. It seems we (Asobo) are as unlucky as Simon. We're crashing in Release and hit a LLVM assert in debug. If using the snippet from Simon, it seems this code is the responsible (it was not crashing before tho). It is also templated code with out variable. We'll keep the old version of dxc for now but it would be great to have a fix of this issue. 

```
template <typename T, typename T2, typename T3>
bool TRayVsAABB(T3 rayOrigin, T3 rayDir, T3 AABBMin, T3 AABBMax, out T2 intersections)
{
	T3 invRayDir = 1.0 / rayDir;
	T3 t0 = (AABBMin - rayOrigin) * invRayDir;
	T3 t1 = (AABBMax - rayOrigin) * invRayDir;
	T3 tmin = min(t0, t1);
	T3 tmax = max(t0, t1);

	T tClose = max(max(tmin.x, tmin.y), tmin.z);
	T tFar = min(min(tmax.x, tmax.y), tmax.z);
	intersections = T2(tClose, tFar);

	return tClose <= tFar;
}
```

Cheers,
Robin.
